  "about": {
    "title": "The tradition continues",
    "body": "Mose Meyers opened the Dublin Barber Shoppe in 1938, offering men traditional haircuts in a traditional setting. Jack Price became a partner in 1967 and later the owner, when Dublin had only 350 residents. His son Craig joined him in 1996 and owns the shop today, where he and his barbers keep giving friendly, precise service."
